---
import StaticPage from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'October 5, 2026';
---

<StaticPage
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How HomelyFusion collects, uses, shares, and protects your information when you visit our site."
	icon="🔒"
>
	<p class="updated" style="margin-top:-1rem;">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

	<p>
		At <strong>HomelyFusion</strong>, your privacy is very important to us. This Privacy Policy outlines the
		types of personal information we collect and how it is used, stored, and protected. Our goal is to be as
		transparent and clear as possible about how we manage your data while providing valuable content and services
		related to bathroom decor, lighting &amp; ambiance, minimalist living, and seasonal home inspiration.
	</p>
	<p>
		By using our website <a href="https://homelyfusion.com">https://homelyfusion.com</a> (the "Site"), you agree
		to the practices described in this Privacy Policy.
	</p>

	<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
	<p>
		HomelyFusion is a content-based platform that provides design inspiration, product recommendations, DIY
		tips, and shopping resources across a variety of home decor categories. We are a
		<strong>for-profit website</strong>, which may generate income through affiliate links, sponsored content,
		display advertising, and product partnerships.
	</p>
	<p>
		We are committed to protecting your personal information and complying with all applicable data protection
		laws, including the <strong>General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)</strong> and the
		<strong>California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA)</strong> where applicable.
	</p>

	<h2>2. What information we collect</h2>
	<p>
		We collect both <strong>personal</strong> and <strong>non-personal</strong> information from visitors to our
		website. This includes:
	</p>

	<h3>a) Information you provide to us</h3>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Name</strong> (if submitted via contact forms or email)</li>
		<li><strong>Email address</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Messages or inquiries</strong> sent through our contact form</li>
		<li><strong>Comments</strong> on blog posts</li>
		<li><strong>Subscription details</strong> (e.g., joining our newsletter)</li>
	</ul>

	<h3>b) Information automatically collected</h3>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>IP address</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Browser type and version</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Pages you visit on our site</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Time spent on each page</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Device type (mobile, desktop, tablet)</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Referring URL (where you came from)</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Clickstream data</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Cookies and usage data</strong> (see Section 6)</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We use tools like <strong>Google Analytics</strong>, <strong>Search Console</strong>, and third-party
		advertising platforms to collect anonymous data about how visitors use the site. This helps us understand what
		content is valuable and how to improve your experience.
	</p>

	<h2>3. How we use your information</h2>
	<p>The information we collect is used for the following purposes:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>To personalize your experience</strong></li>
		<li><strong>To respond to your inquiries or support requests</strong></li>
		<li><strong>To improve our content and site performance</strong></li>
		<li><strong>To send newsletters or promotional emails</strong> (only if you opt-in)</li>
		<li><strong>To analyze traffic trends and user behavior</strong></li>
		<li><strong>To prevent fraudulent activity or abuse</strong></li>
		<li><strong>To display relevant advertising</strong></li>
		<li><strong>To comply with legal obligations</strong></li>
	</ul>
	<p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal data to third parties for commercial gain.</p>

	<h2>4. Legal basis for processing (for European visitors)</h2>
	<p>
		If you are located in the European Economic Area (EEA), our legal basis for collecting and using your
		personal data will depend on the personal data concerned and the specific context in which we collect it.
	</p>
	<p>We will process your personal data only where:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>You have given consent</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Processing is necessary for performance of a contract</strong></li>
		<li><strong>It is required for compliance with legal obligations</strong></li>
		<li><strong>It is necessary for our legitimate interests</strong> (such as improving the website, responding to inquiries, preventing fraud)</li>
	</ul>
	<p>You have the right to withdraw your consent at any time.</p>

	<h2>5. Who we share your information with</h2>
	<p>
		We may share your personal information with the following third parties, solely to support the functioning
		and monetization of HomelyFusion:
	</p>

	<h3>a) Service providers</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>Email marketing platforms (e.g., Mailchimp, ConvertKit)</li>
		<li>Website hosting providers</li>
		<li>Analytics platforms (Google Analytics, Plausible, etc.)</li>
	</ul>

	<h3>b) Advertising &amp; affiliate partners</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>Google AdSense or Mediavine (for display advertising)</li>
		<li>Affiliate programs (e.g., Amazon Associates, ShareASale)</li>
		<li>Sponsored partners (clearly labeled in our content)</li>
	</ul>

	<h3>c) Legal compliance</h3>
	<p>
		We may disclose your data if required to do so by law or in response to valid legal processes, such as
		subpoenas or court orders.
	</p>
	<p><strong>We do not sell or lease your data</strong> to third-party marketers.</p>

	<h2>6. Cookies and tracking technologies</h2>
	<p>
		Like many websites, HomelyFusion uses <strong>cookies and similar technologies</strong> to enhance your
		experience and collect data about your visit.
	</p>

	<h3>What are cookies?</h3>
	<p>
		Cookies are small text files stored on your device to help websites remember your preferences, activity, and
		browsing behavior.
	</p>

	<h3>Types of cookies we use</h3>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Essential Cookies</strong>: Necessary for basic site functionality</li>
		<li><strong>Performance Cookies</strong>: Help us analyze site performance</li>
		<li><strong>Functionality Cookies</strong>: Remember preferences (like dark mode)</li>
		<li><strong>Advertising Cookies</strong>: Deliver personalized ads</li>
	</ul>

	<h3>Third-party cookies</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>Google Analytics</li>
		<li>Facebook Pixel (if enabled)</li>
		<li>Google AdSense or other ad networks</li>
		<li>Affiliate tracking cookies (e.g., Amazon)</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		You can control cookies through your browser settings. Most browsers allow you to block or delete cookies.
		However, disabling cookies may impact your experience on our site.
	</p>

	<h2>7. Email and newsletter communication</h2>
	<p>When you subscribe to our newsletter, we collect your name and email address. We use this information to:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Send you blog updates, product recommendations, and seasonal decor tips</li>
		<li>Share exclusive discounts or affiliate promotions</li>
		<li>Notify you about new features, guides, or giveaways</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		All emails include an <strong>unsubscribe link</strong>, and you may opt out of future communications at any
		time.
	</p>
	<p>
		We use reputable third-party services (e.g., Mailchimp, ConvertKit) to manage subscriptions and track email
		performance.
	</p>

	<h2>8. Affiliate links and advertisements</h2>
	<p>
		As disclosed on our <a href="/disclosure/">Disclosure page</a>, some links on our website are
		<strong>affiliate links</strong>, which means we may earn a commission if you click through and make a
		purchase.
	</p>
	<p>
		These links <strong>do not impact your price or shopping experience</strong>. Affiliate programs we
		participate in include:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Amazon Associates</li>
		<li>CJ Affiliate</li>
		<li>ShareASale</li>
		<li>PartnerStack</li>
		<li>Impact</li>
		<li>Other home-related affiliate networks</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We also display <strong>third-party advertisements</strong>, which may use cookies and tracking to serve
		relevant ads based on your interests.
	</p>
	<p>
		We strive to partner only with advertisers that align with our values in home decor, minimalism, and
		eco-conscious living.
	</p>

	<h2>9. Data retention</h2>
	<p>
		We retain your personal information only for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes outlined in this
		Privacy Policy. For example:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Email subscribers: until you unsubscribe</li>
		<li>Comments: indefinitely unless you request removal</li>
		<li>Analytics data: retained per the platform's standard policy (e.g., 26 months for Google Analytics)</li>
	</ul>
	<p>We periodically audit and delete outdated data to maintain data minimization standards.</p>

	<h2>10. How we protect your data</h2>
	<p>
		HomelyFusion implements <strong>reasonable technical and organizational measures</strong> to protect your data
		from unauthorized access, disclosure, loss, or destruction. These include:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>SSL encryption (HTTPS)</li>
		<li>Regular software updates</li>
		<li>Limiting access to authorized personnel</li>
		<li>Using secure third-party platforms</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		However, no website or internet transmission is 100% secure. While we strive to protect your information, we
		cannot guarantee absolute security.
	</p>
</StaticPage>
